WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.030
Two, three, five, seven, eleven, thirteen.

2
00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:08.340
Along the number line,
the primes keep appearing.

3
00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:12.650
But as the line runs on, the gaps
between them start to stretch.

4
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.210
No computer can check every number.

5
00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:18.230
So could the primes
one day simply run out?

6
00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:20.830
How could you ever prove
they go on forever,

7
00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.790
without writing them all down?

8
00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.700
In this mission, you'll prove a
statement by assuming it is false,

9
00:00:26.750 --> 00:00:29.880
and reasoning until you
hit something impossible.

10
00:00:29.930 --> 00:00:33.450
You'll multiply a list of
primes together and add one.

11
00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.130
Divide that number by
any prime on the list,

12
00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.680
and the remainder is always one.

13
00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:42.350
You'll see why that small
fact is so powerful.

14
00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.520
Your mission: explain how you can
prove the primes never run out,

15
00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:47.650
without a list.
